\subsection{Statistical Significance Analysis via One-Way ANOVA}
Following the statistical evaluation protocol of Noiumkar and Tirakoat \cite{noiumkar2013use}, we conducted a one-way Analysis of Variance (ANOVA) across the four competing architectures ($k=4$ groups, $n=5$ seeds per group, $df_{\text{between}}=3$, $df_{\text{within}}=16$) on MPJPE (mm), as reported in Table \ref{tab:anova_results}. In all eight benchmark scenarios, the $F$-statistics ($417.09 \le F \le 3568.51$) are statistically significant at the $0.001$ level ($p < 0.001$), confirming that the error reductions achieved by KAR-STGCN are highly consistent across random initializations.

