% ============================================================================
\section{Conclusion}
% ============================================================================
This paper presented a Kinematic-Aware Spatio-Temporal Graph Convolutional Network (KAR-STGCN) paired with a visibility-guarded wrist-centered $L_2$ palm-bone normalization scheme for 3D hand skeletal restoration and gesture recognition. By addressing both optical burst dropouts and anatomical bone-ratio mismatches \cite{noiumkar2013use}, our method outperforms kinematic filtering, Bi-LSTM, and 1D-TCN baselines across all four degradation levels while operating in real time ($<0.48\text{ ms}$) on an NVIDIA GeForce RTX 2050 GPU.

